IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-pilot-earnings`

-- Tests of er5-pilot-earnings (regs 77.8, 77.94, 77.95, 77.97 and 77.99). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Regulations
-- (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1460-1465, 1513-1518, 1521-1527, 1542-1548 and 1562-1568), beside each assertion, before the run.
-- Which day of the week a date is was checked against Python's datetime: Aug 6, 2011, Aug 4, 2012, Aug 1, 2015, Aug 6, 2016 and Aug 11, 2018 are Saturdays; the windows begin on Sundays.

§ `Purposes (src:1460, 1513, 1521, 1542, 1562)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.8(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 12` EQUALS "testing whether increasing the amount of a claimant’s allowable earnings from employment while the claimant is receiving benefits would encourage more claimants to accept employment while receiving benefits"
#ASSERT `reg 77.94(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 17` EQUALS "testing whether increasing the amount of a claimant’s allowable earnings from employment while the claimant is receiving benefits would encourage more claimants to accept employment while receiving benefits"
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 18` EQUALS "testing whether deducting from benefits payable to any claimant who has earnings during a week of unemployment 50% of those earnings, until the earnings exceed 90% of their weekly insurable earnings, would encourage claimants to work more while receiving benefits"
#ASSERT `reg 77.97(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 19` EQUALS "testing whether deducting from benefits payable to any claimant who has earnings during a week of unemployment 50% of those earnings, until the earnings exceed 90% of their weekly insurable earnings, would encourage claimants to work more while receiving benefits"
#ASSERT `reg 77.99(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 20` EQUALS "testing whether deducting from benefits payable to any claimant who has earnings during a week of unemployment 50% of those earnings, until the earnings are greater than 90% of their weekly insurable earnings, would encourage claimants to work more while receiving benefits"

§ `The week and the cessation of the section (src:1465, 1518, 1527, 1548, 1568)`

-- The section ceases to have effect on Saturday August 6, 2011: the week of Sunday July 31, 2011 ends that day and is in; the week of Sunday August 7, 2011 is out.
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(4) the section has effect for the week` (YearMonthDay 2011 7 31) (YearMonthDay 2011 8 6)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.8(4) the section has effect for the week` (YearMonthDay 2011 8 7) (YearMonthDay 2011 8 6))
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(4) the section has effect for the week` (YearMonthDay 2011 7 24) (YearMonthDay 2011 8 6)

§ `Reg 77.8(2) - who is included in Pilot Project No. 12 (src:1461)`

-- The argument order is: the day the benefit period is established; the day it ends, if it has; resident in a region described in Schedule I.
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2008 12 7) NOTHING TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2008 12 6) NOTHING TRUE)
-- Established the day before the period but ending on its first day: included ("established or ends").
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2008 12 6) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 12 7)) TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2011 8 6) NOTHING TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2011 8 7) NOTHING TRUE)
-- Established before the period and ending after it: neither event falls in the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2008 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1)) TRUE)
-- Not resident in a region described in Schedule I.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) NOTHING FALSE)

§ `Reg 77.8(3) and 77.94(3) - the maximum allowable earnings (src:1462-1464, 1515-1517)`

-- (a) $75 if the rate of weekly benefits is less than $188; (b) 40% of the rate if it is $188 or more.
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) and reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings` 187 EQUALS 75
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) and reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings` 0 EQUALS 75
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) and reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings` 188 EQUALS 75.2
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) and reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings` 200 EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) and reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings` 300 EQUALS 120
-- For the week of Sunday July 31, 2011, in Pilot Project No. 12: 40% of 200. For the week of Sunday August 7, 2011 the section has ceased to have effect: NOTHING.
-- The argument order is: included; the Sunday that begins the week; the rate of weekly benefits.
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 12` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 7 31) 200 EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 12` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 7 31) 187 EQUALS JUST 75
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 12` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 8 7) 200 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 77.8(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 12` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2011 7 31) 200 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77.9 - repealed (src:1466)`

-- The stub is documentation with a section number: a string carrying the text's own words.
#ASSERT `reg 77.9 is repealed and therefore not encoded` EQUALS "77.9 [Repealed, SOR/2016-206, s. 8]"

§ `Reg 77.94 - Pilot Project No. 17 (src:1513-1518)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.94(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 17` (YearMonthDay 2011 8 7) NOTHING TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.94(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 17` (YearMonthDay 2011 8 6) NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 77.94(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 17` (YearMonthDay 2011 8 6) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2011 8 7)) TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 77.94(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 17` (YearMonthDay 2012 8 4) NOTHING TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.94(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 17` (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5) NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.94(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 17` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) NOTHING FALSE)
-- The section ceases to have effect on Saturday August 4, 2012: the week of Sunday July 29, 2012 is in; the week of Sunday August 5, 2012 is out.
#ASSERT `reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 17` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2012 7 29) 200 EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT `reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 17` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5) 200 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 17` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 7 29) 200 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regs 77.95, 77.97, 77.99 (2) - who is included (src:1522, 1543, 1563)`

-- The argument order is: the Sunday that begins the week for which the claim is made; resident in a region described in Schedule I.
-- Pilot Project No. 18: the weeks from Sunday August 5, 2012 to Saturday August 1, 2015.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 18` (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.95(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 18` (YearMonthDay 2012 7 29) TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 18` (YearMonthDay 2015 7 26) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.95(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 18` (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.95(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 18` (YearMonthDay 2013 1 6) FALSE)
-- Pilot Project No. 19: the weeks from Sunday August 2, 2015 to Saturday August 6, 2016.
#ASSERT `reg 77.97(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 19` (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.97(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 19` (YearMonthDay 2015 7 26) TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 77.97(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 19` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.97(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 19` (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.97(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 19` (YearMonthDay 2016 1 3) FALSE)
-- Pilot Project No. 20: the weeks from Sunday August 7, 2016 to Saturday August 11, 2018.
#ASSERT `reg 77.99(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 20` (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.99(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 20` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 31) TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 77.99(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 20` (YearMonthDay 2018 8 5) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.99(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 20` (YearMonthDay 2018 8 12) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.99(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 20` (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1) FALSE)

§ `Regs 77.95(3), 77.97(3), 77.99(3) - the adapted subsection 19(2.1) (src:1523-1524, 1544-1545, 1564-1565)`

-- With a weekly insurable earnings figure of 500, the threshold is 90% of it, 450.
-- The argument order is: the earnings of the week; the weekly insurable earnings used to establish the rate; the deduction is for the purpose of section 13.
-- Earnings of 300 are below the threshold: 50% of 300 is 150.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted under subsection 19(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 300 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 150
-- Earnings of 450, exactly the threshold: 50% of 450 is 225.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted under subsection 19(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 450 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 225
-- One dollar over: 50% of the first 450 and all of the 1: 226.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted under subsection 19(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 451 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 226
-- Earnings of 600: 50% of 450 is 225, and 100% of the 150 above it: 375.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted under subsection 19(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 600 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 375
-- No earnings: nothing to deduct.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted under subsection 19(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 0 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- For the purpose of section 13 the added subsection does not govern.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted under subsection 19(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 600 500 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regs 77.95(4), 77.97(4), 77.99(4) - the adapted subsection 152.18(2.1) (src:1525-1526, 1546-1547, 1566-1567)`

-- The argument order is: the earnings of the week; the sum of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b); the deduction is for the purpose of section 152.15.
-- A sum of 26,000 divided by 52 is 500: the same figures as above.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(4), reg 77.97(4) and reg 77.99(4) the amount to be deducted under subsection 152.18(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 600 26000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 375
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(4), reg 77.97(4) and reg 77.99(4) the amount to be deducted under subsection 152.18(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 300 26000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 150
-- A sum of 20,800 divided by 52 is 400: the threshold is 360. Earnings of 500: 50% of 360 is 180, and 100% of 140: 320.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(4), reg 77.97(4) and reg 77.99(4) the amount to be deducted under subsection 152.18(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 500 20800 FALSE EQUALS JUST 320
-- For the purpose of section 152.15 the added subsection does not govern.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(4), reg 77.97(4) and reg 77.99(4) the amount to be deducted under subsection 152.18(2.1) of the Act as adapted` 600 26000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regs 77.95(5), 77.97(5), 77.99(5) - the sections cease to have effect (src:1527, 1548, 1568)`

-- The argument order is: the claimant is included; the Sunday that begins the week.
-- Pilot Project No. 18 ceases to have effect on Saturday August 1, 2015: the week of Sunday July 26, 2015 is in.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(5) Pilot Project No. 18 governs the deduction for the week` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 7 26)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.95(5) Pilot Project No. 18 governs the deduction for the week` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.95(5) Pilot Project No. 18 governs the deduction for the week` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2015 7 26))
#ASSERT `reg 77.97(5) Pilot Project No. 19 governs the deduction for the week` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 7 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.97(5) Pilot Project No. 19 governs the deduction for the week` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.97(5) Pilot Project No. 19 governs the deduction for the week` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2016 7 31))
#ASSERT `reg 77.99(5) Pilot Project No. 20 governs the deduction for the week` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2018 8 5)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.99(5) Pilot Project No. 20 governs the deduction for the week` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2018 8 12))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.99(5) Pilot Project No. 20 governs the deduction for the week` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2018 8 5))

§ `Whichever of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the week (src:1522-1527, 1543-1548, 1563-1568)`

-- The argument order is: the Sunday that begins the week; resident in a region described in Schedule I.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5) and reg 77.99(5) one of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the deduction for the week` (YearMonthDay 2013 1 6) TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5) and reg 77.99(5) one of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the deduction for the week` (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2) TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5) and reg 77.99(5) one of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the deduction for the week` (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7) TRUE
-- The week of Sunday August 12, 2018 is after all three; the week of Sunday July 29, 2012 is before them.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5) and reg 77.99(5) one of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the deduction for the week` (YearMonthDay 2018 8 12) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5) and reg 77.99(5) one of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the deduction for the week` (YearMonthDay 2012 7 29) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5) and reg 77.99(5) one of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the deduction for the week` (YearMonthDay 2013 1 6) FALSE)
-- The deduction: the argument order is: one of the projects governs; the earnings; the weekly insurable earnings (500); the deduction is for the purpose of section 13.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted for the week under whichever pilot project governs` TRUE 600 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 375
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted for the week under whichever pilot project governs` FALSE 600 500 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted for the week under whichever pilot project governs` TRUE 600 500 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The self-employed person's deduction: the argument order is: one of the projects governs; the earnings; the sum of the amounts of paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) (26,000, divided by 52 is 500); for the purpose of section 152.15.
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(4), reg 77.97(4) and reg 77.99(4) the amount to be deducted for the week under whichever pilot project governs` TRUE 600 26000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 375
#ASSERT `reg 77.95(4), reg 77.97(4) and reg 77.99(4) the amount to be deducted for the week under whichever pilot project governs` FALSE 600 26000 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
